[51.953, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H    ▎+ import unittest                                                                                              \n    ▎ \n    ▎+ from fib import fib                                                                                          \n    ▎+                                                                                                              \n    ▎+                                                                                                              \n    ▎+ class TestFib(unittest.TestCase):                                                                            \n    ▎+     def test_known_values(self):                                                                             \n    ▎+         cases = [(0, 0), (1, 1), (2, 1), (10, 55)]                                                           \n    ▎+         for n, expected in cases:                                                                            \n    ▎+             with self.subTest(n=n):                                                                          \n    ▎+                 self.assertEqual(fib(n), expected)                                                           \n    ▎+                                                                                                              \n    ▎ … truncated (11 more lines) · ctrl+r to review\n\n  $ cd /private/var/folders/5w/xh9wzz_j7l14jcqmty0hf6rm0000gp/T/codeterm-state-capture-cursor-working-idle-2-54181 &&\n    python -m unittest test_fib.py -v exit 127 • 443ms\n    (eval):1: command not found: python\n\n  $ cd /private/var/folders/5w/xh9wzz_j7l14jcqmty0hf6rm0000gp/T/codeterm-state-capture-cursor-working-idle-2-54181 &&\n    python3 -m unittest test_fib.py -v 841ms\n    … 5 output lines hidden · ctrl+o to expand\n    OK\n\n  Here’s what changed:\n\n  fib.py — input validation before computing:\n  • TypeError if n is not an integer (including floats, strings, and booleans)\n  • ValueErr